# Secret keys

A key names the value. Use kebab-case: `client-secret`, `tunnel-token`, `access-key-id`, `cookie-secret`.

A bare word is not a key. `password`, `username`, `token`, `url`, `region`, and `cloud` do not say which value they hold.

Keep a key the consumer will not read under another name, and comment that constraint. CloudNativePG reads `username` and `password` on a `kubernetes.io/basic-auth` secret. The Velero chart mounts the credentials file from the key `cloud`.

Rename a key in the same change as every `secretKeyRef`, `valuesKey`, and `apiTokenSecretRef` that reads it.
